  30:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c **** 
  31:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c **** /**
  32:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * @ingroup groupTransforms
  33:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  */
  34:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c **** 
  35:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c **** /**
  36:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * @defgroup DCT4_IDCT4 DCT Type IV Functions
  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * Representation of signals by minimum number of values is important for storage and transmission.
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * The possibility of large discontinuity between the beginning and end of a period of a signal
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * in DFT can be avoided by extending the signal so that it is even-symmetric.
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * Discrete Cosine Transform (DCT) is constructed such that its energy is heavily concentrated in t
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * spectrum and is very widely used in signal and image coding applications.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * The family of DCTs (DCT type- 1,2,3,4) is the outcome of different combinations of homogeneous b
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * DCT has an excellent energy-packing capability, hence has many applications and in data compress
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  *
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * DCT is essentially the Discrete Fourier Transform(DFT) of an even-extended real signal.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * Reordering of the input data makes the computation of DCT just a problem of
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * computing the DFT of a real signal with a few additional operations.
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * This approach provides regular, simple, and very efficient DCT algorithms for practical hardware
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  *
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * DCT type-II can be implemented using Fast fourier transform (FFT) internally, as the transform i
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * DCT4 is implemented using DCT2 as their implementations are similar except with some added pre-p
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * DCT2 implementation can be described in the following steps:
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * - Re-ordering input
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * - Calculating Real FFT
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * - Multiplication of weights and Real FFT output and getting real part from the product.
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  *
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * This process is explained by the block diagram below:
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \image html DCT4.gif "Discrete Cosine Transform - type-IV"
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  *
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \par Algorithm:
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * The N-point type-IV DCT is defined as a real, linear transformation by the formula:
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \image html DCT4Equation.gif
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * where <code>k = 0,1,2,.....N-1</code>
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  *\par
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * Its inverse is defined as follows:
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \image html IDCT4Equation.gif
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * where <code>n = 0,1,2,.....N-1</code>
  68:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  *\par
  69:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * The DCT4 matrices become involutory (i.e. they are self-inverse) by multiplying with an overall 
  70:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * The symmetry of the transform matrix indicates that the fast algorithms for the forward
  71:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * and inverse transform computation are identical.
  72:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * Note that the implementation of Inverse DCT4 and DCT4 is same, hence same process function can b
  73:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  *
  74:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \par Lengths supported by the transform:
  75:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  *  As DCT4 internally uses Real FFT, it supports all the lengths 128, 512, 2048 and 8192.
  76:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * The library provides separate functions for Q15, Q31, and floating-point data types.
  77:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \par Instance Structure
  78:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * The instances for Real FFT and FFT, cosine values table and twiddle factor table are stored in a
  79:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * A separate instance structure must be defined for each transform.
  80:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * There are separate instance structure declarations for each of the 3 supported data types.
  81:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  *
  82:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \par Initialization Functions
  83:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * There is also an associated initialization function for each data type.
  84:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * The initialization function performs the following operations:
  85:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * - Sets the values of the internal structure fields.
  86:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * - Initializes Real FFT as its process function is used internally in DCT4, by calling arm_rfft_i
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\cc4enYWt.s 			page 3


  87:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \par
  88:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * Use of the initialization function is optional.
  89:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * However, if the initialization function is used, then the instance structure cannot be placed in
  90:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * To place an instance structure into a const data section, the instance structure must be manuall
  91:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * Manually initialize the instance structure as follows:
  92:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * <pre>
  93:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  *arm_dct4_instance_f32 S = {N, Nby2, normalize, pTwiddle, pCosFactor, pRfft, pCfft};
  94:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  *arm_dct4_instance_q31 S = {N, Nby2, normalize, pTwiddle, pCosFactor, pRfft, pCfft};
  95:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  *arm_dct4_instance_q15 S = {N, Nby2, normalize, pTwiddle, pCosFactor, pRfft, pCfft};
  96:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * </pre>
  97:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * where \c N is the length of the DCT4; \c Nby2 is half of the length of the DCT4;
  98:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \c normalize is normalizing factor used and is equal to <code>sqrt(2/N)</code>;
  99:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \c pTwiddle points to the twiddle factor table;
 100:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \c pCosFactor points to the cosFactor table;
 101:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \c pRfft points to the real FFT instance;
 102:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \c pCfft points to the complex FFT instance;
 103:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * The CFFT and RFFT structures also needs to be initialized, refer to arm_cfft_radix4_f32()
 104:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * and arm_rfft_f32() respectively for details regarding static initialization.
 105:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  *
 106:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * \par Fixed-Point Behavior
 107:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * Care must be taken when using the fixed-point versions of the DCT4 transform functions.
 108:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * In particular, the overflow and saturation behavior of the accumulator used in each function mus
 109:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * Refer to the function specific documentation below for usage guidelines.
 110:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  */
 111:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c **** 
 112:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  /**
 113:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/TransformFunctions/arm_dct4_f32.c ****  * @addtogroup DCT4_IDCT4
